Statement: "A test that pauses request A right after its SELECT, lets request B run its SELECT, and then runs both to the end fails on the shipped code (two rotated results with different tokens) and passes after the fix (one rotated, one grace with the same token)."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The test forces the exact interleaving from C instead of hoping the timing happens: both reads before any write. On the shipped code both requests rotate and the family forks; after the compare-and-swap fix only one UPDATE returns a row, and the loser, from the same device inside the window, gets the winner''s successor. A test that fires two real requests and hopes they overlap passes or fails depending on timing, which is why the scheduler pauses at a named statement: the same interleaving every run.', 6, 5
