-- challenge chal_coding_nas_322 (fix_bug)
INSERT INTO challenge.challenges (public_id, course_id, module_id, lesson_id, name, title, description, status, difficulty, type, points, is_published, is_deleted)
VALUES ('chal_coding_nas_322', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'nodejs-api-security'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'nodejs-api-security') AND order_index = 3 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-nas-3-2' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'concurrent-refresh-compare-and-swap', 'Concurrent Refresh', 'When the CodeDev phone app resumes, two requests can call POST /auth/refresh with the same refresh token 40 ms apart. In production both answered 200 with two different tokens, and on the next refresh the phone was flagged as a replay and the learner was signed out on every device. Fix refresh() so that, however the statements of concurrent requests interleave, exactly one request rotates the token.

Required results: the winner gets {status:"rotated", token}; a request that lost the race, comes from the row''s device and is less than GRACE_MS = 10000 ms after the row''s usedAt gets the winner''s successor {status:"grace", token} and nothing new is issued; if the winner has not recorded its successor yet (replacedBy still null) the loser gets {status:"retry"} (the API answers 409 and the client tries again 100 ms later), with no revocation and no event. A reuse from another device, after the window, or after the successor was used is still a replay: revoke the family, record one refresh_token_reuse event and return {status:"replay_detected"}. Invalid, revoked and expired tokens keep their answers, and a winner whose family was revoked meanwhile (issue returns null) answers "revoked". Issue a successor only for the request that won.

Each Db method is one atomic SQL statement, listed in the store; markUsed is UPDATE refresh_tokens SET used_at = $2 WHERE id = $1 AND used_at IS NULL AND revoked_at IS NULL RETURNING *. The test runner is a deterministic scheduler: a step {op:"concurrent", requests:[{id, token, device, at}], schedule:[["A","findByHash"], ["B","findByHash"], ["A","end"], ...]} runs request A until it completes its next findByHash statement, then B, and so on; unfinished requests then run to the end in order. Tokens are labels ("t2" = the token of row r2), "@A" (the token last returned to request A) or literal strings. Output: one line per request ("B refresh t1 phone @900040: grace t2"), then the security events and every row ("r1 f1 phone used=900000 revoked=- next=r2"); with "quiet": true, a summary.', 'open', 'hard'::difficulty_question, 'fix_bug', 40, true, false)
