       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nas_322'), 2, 'Look at the rotation step in refresh(): the check `row.usedAt !== null` uses a copy read earlier, and retireLiveTokens updates whatever is live in the family when it runs. The store has a statement whose result tells you whether you were the one who changed used_at. Then look at what handleReuse does when the successor is not recorded yet.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nas_322'), 3, 'A similar race on different data: two requests redeem the same one-time voucher. `SELECT used FROM vouchers WHERE code = $1` then `UPDATE vouchers SET used = true WHERE code = $1` lets both pass. `UPDATE vouchers SET used = true WHERE code = $1 AND used = false RETURNING id` returns a row to exactly one of them; the other reads the voucher again and answers from what the winner left (here: the order it created, or ''try again'' if the order is not saved yet).');
