    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nas_331'), 'Response from https://app.codedev.test after sign-in:
Set-Cookie: sid=9f2c...; Path=/; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax

A page on https://free-certs.example, opened by a signed-in learner in a current Chrome or Firefox:
<form method="POST" action="https://app.codedev.test/settings/email">
  <input type="hidden" name="email" value="owner@free-certs.example">
</form>
<script>document.forms[0].submit()</script>

Statement: "The browser sends this cross-site POST without the sid cookie, so the server handles it as a request from a signed-out visitor."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. free-certs.example and codedev.test are different sites, and SameSite=Lax withholds the cookie on cross-site requests except top-level navigations with a safe method such as GET. A form POST is a top-level navigation with an unsafe method, so sid is not attached. Two limits keep CSRF defences necessary anyway: Lax still sends the cookie on a cross-site GET navigation (so a GET that changes state is exposed), and SameSite does nothing against a page on another subdomain of codedev.test, which is the same site. Chrome''s temporary exception that sends cookies on cross-site POSTs applies only to cookies set without a SameSite attribute, not to an explicit Lax.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nas_331') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
