    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nas_331'), 'Response header on https://app.codedev.test:
Content-Security-Policy: default-src ''self''; script-src ''self''; object-src ''none''; base-uri ''none''

The stored comment <img src="x" onerror="fetch(''/settings/email'', ...)"> still reaches the DOM through innerHTML, and the image fails to load.

Statement: "With this policy, the browser does not run the onerror handler and reports a Content-Security-Policy violation in the console."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. An inline event handler is inline script. script-src ''self'' allows script files from the page''s own origin but no inline code, because it has neither ''unsafe-inline'' nor a hash or nonce that matches. The image request is allowed (a same-origin URL), it fails, and the browser refuses to execute the handler, logging a violation such as "Refused to execute inline event handler because it violates the following Content Security Policy directive". CSP is a second line of defence: the comment is still injected HTML and must be fixed at the source by sanitising or escaping it, and a policy with ''unsafe-inline'' would have let the handler run.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nas_331') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
